@@ -46,3 +46,18 @@ other value replaces or recursively merges it. A non-object patch (including an
 the whole target. Notes: arrays are replaced, never merged; `null` cannot be set as a value; a non-object
 target is treated as `{}` when the patch is an object; `"__proto__"` and similar are ordinary keys. It
 never throws.
+
+## Creating a patch
+
+```ts
+import { createPatch } from "./src/index.js";
+
+createPatch({ a: [1, 2, 3], b: 1 }, { a: [1, 3], b: 1 }); // [{ op: "remove", path: "/a/1" }]
+```
+
+`createPatch(from, to)` returns a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) that `applyPatch` turns from `from` into `to`. It
+describes only what changed: unchanged members and items are left alone, nested changes get their own
+path, and an array item that is inserted or deleted is a single `add` or `remove` (items are matched by
+deep equality, so the items around it are not rewritten). A moved array item is a `remove` plus an `add`.
+Only `add`, `remove` and `replace` are emitted. Neither input is mutated and the patch shares no structure
+with them.
